    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0207" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/497.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 80.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your despatch No. 159 of March 18 and your No. 165 of March 24, regarding claims
                    against the Chinese Government growing out of the revolution of 1911–1912.</p>
                <p>In the event of the British and German Governments, or either of them, expressing
                    their willingness to refuse definitely to present to China claims for indirect
                    losses, such as are set forth in the summary sent with your No. 165 of certain
                    claims received by the Legation, you are instructed to refuse to present such
                    claims.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cone Johnson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
